Renderer start failure: the window says why instead of a frozen magenta screen. The GS renderer is the only renderer, and
when it cannot start (no OpenGL 4.3 core context: old GPU, the Microsoft Basic Display Adapter, Remote Desktop; or a
driver that rejects the shaders) no frame ever arrives and the window kept its magenta placeholder: players reported
"a pink screen, frozen". The renderer records the reason (GSSharedPresent::SetRendererFailure) and the host window draws
a short explanation in the launcher's language (TOBIICHI_IDIOMA en/es/pt; ASCII, raylib's default font). Nothing
changes while the renderer works. GOW_GS_FAIL_TEST=context|shaders (test) fails the start on purpose.
Checked on an RX 580: both test failures show their message (es, pt; long lines shrink to fit 1920x1080), and a normal
run shows the title screen as before.

